WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:12.200
Find this fictional company’s supplier bills on the records board.

2
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:30.440
The bills show rule-based coding, an AI suggestion and a tax-check exception.

3
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:42.880
The rule-coded bill carries its account, tax and total checks for approval.

4
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:49.400
Finance maintains the coding rules on a records board.

5
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:58.640
Fixed workflow steps apply the rules before requesting an AI suggestion.

6
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:20.400
An uncovered bill line receives a labelled AI coding suggestion.

7
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:31.680
The AI suggestion waits for a recorded review and correction.

8
00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:38.080
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the AP clerk.

9
00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:44.320
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the AP clerk: change the cost centre.

10
00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:54.400
The automated AP-clerk role marks the correction and saves it.

11
00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.440
Saving the correction starts the board’s recheck workflow.

12
00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:20.680
The recheck validates the correction against the current coding controls.

13
00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:31.560
The corrected bill becomes the current checked version for approval.

14
00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:41.020
The bill note keeps the AI suggestion beside the recorded correction.

15
00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:50.940
The selected AI step shows its suggestion for the uncovered line.

16
00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:56.260
The bank-lines board holds fictional receipts for matching.

17
00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:04.420
Find the fictional receipts used in this workflow.

18
00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:22.500
Matching uses the customer, invoice reference and receipt amount.

19
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:34.700
The short payment proposes part-payment and keeps the remaining balance open.

20
00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:40.020
The decisions board holds the item and version for finance review.

21
00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:56.580
Find the recorded decisions for these fictional bills and receipts.

22
00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:09.460
The decision record explains why finance needs the current bill version.

23
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:14.980
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the finance controller.

24
00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:24.100
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the finance controller.

25
00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:29.180
The automated finance-controller role selects Approve.

26
00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:39.140
The note records the reason for leaving the remaining balance open.

27
00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:41.620
Saving the automated decision starts the posting workflow.

28
00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:48.020
Open the fictional invoices to see the remaining amounts.

29
00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:57.060
The fictional invoice is part paid, with its remaining balance still open.
